comments:
Looks like it's not limited to `dynamic_date_formats` but also when using `copy_to`, we hit this issue because we had a lingering old template lying around which both matched the index name.

Reproduction case:
```
PUT _template/elasticsearch-2
{
  "index_patterns" : [
    "elasticsearch-2*"
  ],
  "mappings" : {
    "properties" : {
      "cluster_id" : {
        "ignore_above" : 1024,
        "type" : "keyword"
      },
      "cluster_name" : {
        "copy_to" : [
          "cluster_id",
          "ece.cluster"
        ],
        "ignore_above" : 1024,
        "type" : "keyword"
      },
      "ece" : {
        "properties" : {
          "cluster" : {
            "ignore_above" : 1024,
            "type" : "keyword"
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

PUT _template/elasticsearch
{
  "index_patterns" : [
    "elasticsearch-2*"
  ],
  "mappings" : {
    "properties" : {
      "cluster_id" : {
        "type" : "keyword",
        "ignore_above" : 1024
      },
      "cluster_name" : {
        "type" : "keyword",
        "ignore_above" : 1024,
        "copy_to" : [
          "cluster_id",
          "ece.cluster"
        ]
      },
      "ece" : {
        "properties" : {
          "cluster" : {
            "ignore_above" : 1024,
            "type" : "keyword"
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

PUT elasticsearch-2-test
Fails with
{
  "error" : {
    "root_cause" : [
      {
        "type" : "class_cast_exception",
        "reason" : "class java.lang.String cannot be cast to class java.util.Map (java.lang.String and java.util.Map are in module java.base of loader 'bootstrap')"
      }
    ],
    "type" : "class_cast_exception",
    "reason" : "class java.lang.String cannot be cast to class java.util.Map (java.lang.String and java.util.Map are in module java.base of loader 'bootstrap')"
  },
  "status" : 500
}
```

If I remove `cluster_name` (which uses copy_to) in either template, it works.
